## About Yosemite

Yosemite National Park is a beautiful national park in California.
It is known for its mountains, waterfalls, forests, meadows, and giant sequoia trees.

Yosemite was first protected in 1864 and became a national park in 1890.
The park covers nearly 1,200 square miles and attracts visitors who enjoy 
hiking, camping, photography, and exploring nature

## Famous Places in Yosemite

## Half Dome

![Half Dome](https://wallpaperaccess.com/full/2286855.jpg)

Half Dome is one of Yosemite's most recongnizable landmarks. It is a huge 
granite formation that rises nearly 5,000 feet above Yosemite Valley.

### Yosemite Falls

![Yosemite Falls](https://travpedia.net/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Yosemite-National-Park_11zon.webp)

Yosemite Falls is one of the most famous waterfalls in the park. The entire 
water fall drops about 2,425 feet.

### El Capitan

![El Capitan](https://wallpaperaccess.com/full/1406532.jpg)
El Capitan is a massive granite cliff in Yosemite Valley. Its is especially 
well known for rock climbing.

## Wildlife

Yosemite is home to many different animals. Visitors may see black bears, 
deer, coyotes, foxes, squirrels, and many types of birds.

It is important to respect wildlife and keep a safe distance from animals.

